This is Harry Bayliss.

995
00:37:54,167 --> 00:37:55,067
- Yeah, just like,

996
00:37:55,167 --> 00:37:56,200
"It's a Wonderful Life,"
Harry Bailey.

997
00:37:56,300 --> 00:37:57,400
Yeah, very funny.

998
00:37:57,500 --> 00:37:58,400
- Snookums.

999
00:37:58,500 --> 00:37:59,933
- Well, that's a little quick,
isn't it?

1000
00:38:01,067 --> 00:38:01,967
Oh, yeah, sure.

1001
00:38:02,067 --> 00:38:03,733
We could rehearse
all day, yeah.

1002
00:38:03,833 --> 00:38:05,000
- But we won't.
I'm too old for that.

1003
00:38:05,100 --> 00:38:06,833
- Oh no, don't worry.
We'll be there.

1004
00:38:06,933 --> 00:38:08,900
Yeah, thank you very much.

1005
00:38:09,000 --> 00:38:10,400
- Boy, he's a tough negotiator.

1006
00:38:10,500 --> 00:38:12,000
- Mm-hm.

1007
00:38:12,100 --> 00:38:15,200
- Kid, I got you
a $100 lifetime deal.

1008
00:38:15,300 --> 00:38:16,733
- Come on, kids,
break it up.

1009
00:38:16,833 --> 00:38:18,800
- Huh?
- What do you think, Eddie?

1010
00:38:18,900 --> 00:38:20,033
- About what?

1011
00:38:20,133 --> 00:38:21,733
- What's the matter, Eddie,
weren't you listening?

1012
00:38:21,833 --> 00:38:22,900
- Dah-huh?

1013
00:38:23,000 --> 00:38:25,400
- Eddie, looks like
you're an overnight sensation.

1014
00:38:25,500 --> 00:38:26,567
- And it hasn't
even been overnight.

1015
00:38:26,667 --> 00:38:28,233
- ...recorded all night
for immediate release.

1016
00:38:28,333 --> 00:38:29,267
- No kidding. Me?

1017
00:38:29,367 --> 00:38:30,867
- Yeah, do you know
what that means?

1018
00:38:30,967 --> 00:38:32,733
If you hit--
- I'll need more socks?

1019
00:38:32,833 --> 00:38:34,200
- ...top show.

1020
00:38:34,300 --> 00:38:36,000
And then
when you're ready for it,

1021
00:38:36,100 --> 00:38:37,500
the "Eddie Crane Show."

1022
00:38:37,600 --> 00:38:38,733
- Then, "Eddie's World."

1023
00:38:38,833 --> 00:38:39,900
- So quick.

1024
00:38:40,000 --> 00:38:41,267
- Well, that's the way
it happens in this business.

1025
00:38:41,367 --> 00:38:43,267
Sometimes it's fast
or not at all.

1026
00:38:43,367 --> 00:38:44,600
- Yeah, I see what you mean.

1027
00:38:44,700 --> 00:38:46,400
- But don't kid yourself, son.
- You're not that good.

1028
00:38:46,500 --> 00:38:48,500
- It's gonna mean
an awful lot of hard work.

1029
00:38:48,600 --> 00:38:49,833
And I hope you're up to it.

1030
00:38:49,933 --> 00:38:50,967
- Mr. Bayliss,
all my life,

1031
00:38:51,067 --> 00:38:52,333
I've been kicked around
for nothing.

1032
00:38:52,433 --> 00:38:54,167
I ain't afraid of working
to get some place.

1033
00:38:54,267 --> 00:38:55,367
- Thanks, son.

1034
00:38:55,467 --> 00:38:57,067
I know you won't
let anybody down.

1035
00:38:57,167 --> 00:38:58,200
- No, sir.

1036
00:38:58,300 --> 00:39:00,200
- Mind my hinder.

1037
00:39:00,300 --> 00:39:02,267
- How long we supposed to cool
our heels out there, man?

1038
00:39:02,367 --> 00:39:03,600
- Moon, do you hear the news?
I'm gonna make records.

1039
00:39:03,700 --> 00:39:05,233
- No kiddin'?
- Yeah, ain't I, Mr. Bayliss?

1040
00:39:05,333 --> 00:39:06,933
- That's right.
- Yahoo!

1041
00:39:07,033 --> 00:39:07,933
- Yeah, that's crazy.

1042
00:39:08,033 --> 00:39:09,967
- Hey, this calls
for a celebration.

1043
00:39:10,067 --> 00:39:12,300
Come on, let's shake
this town up tonight.

1044
00:39:12,400 --> 00:39:14,533
- Now, hold on here,
just a minute.

1045
00:39:14,633 --> 00:39:16,067
Now, I know you're all
happy about this

1046
00:39:16,167 --> 00:39:18,633
but Eddie's
got to get some rest.

1047
00:39:18,733 --> 00:39:20,567
He's recording
tomorrow night, you know?

1048
00:39:20,667 --> 00:39:23,433
- What you talkin' about?
My Eddie's a big star now.

1049
00:39:23,533 --> 00:39:24,867
He don't have to worry
about singing.

1050
00:39:24,967 --> 00:39:27,367
He can do it with his eyes
closed, can't you, honey?

1051
00:39:27,467 --> 00:39:28,400
- Yeah, I feel fine.

1052
00:39:28,500 --> 00:39:30,300
- Yeah, I think
Mr. Bayliss is right.

1053
00:39:30,400 --> 00:39:32,700
There'll be plenty of time
to celebrate later on.

1054
00:39:32,800 --> 00:39:34,167
You could catch cold
or something.

1055
00:39:34,267 --> 00:39:35,833
- And drive to Houston.
- What are you, his mother?

1056
00:39:35,933 --> 00:39:38,467
- I didn't mean--
- Iris! Maybe they're right.

1057
00:39:38,567 --> 00:39:40,667
I got to protect my voice.
- Well, pick up a neckerchief.

1058
00:39:40,767 --> 00:39:42,167
- Or maybe we just ain't
good enough for you now.

1059
00:39:42,267 --> 00:39:45,033
Is that it?
- Shut up all of you!

1060
00:39:45,133 --> 00:39:46,733
I ain't walkin' out on nobody.
It's just--

1061
00:39:46,833 --> 00:39:48,200
- It's just
that I love pancakes.

1062
00:39:48,300 --> 00:39:49,433
- Oh, I don't know.

1063
00:39:49,533 --> 00:39:50,967
Come on, let's go back
to the hotel.

1064
00:39:51,067 --> 00:39:52,633
I'll see you tomorrow.
- Eddie?

1065
00:39:52,733 --> 00:39:54,200
- Yeah?

1066
00:39:54,300 --> 00:39:55,333
- Good luck.

1067
00:39:55,433 --> 00:39:57,300
- Yeah, thanks.
- Let's go, baby.

1068
00:39:59,833 --> 00:40:00,733
- Helen?

1069
00:40:00,833 --> 00:40:03,900
- Hayes, Gurley Brown,
Keller, Wheels?

1070
00:40:04,000 --> 00:40:07,800
- That sofa's actually
a seat of a pick-up truck.

1071
00:40:07,900 --> 00:40:08,967
[♪♪♪]

1072
00:40:09,067 --> 00:40:10,067
- When in Hollywood,

1073
00:40:10,167 --> 00:40:11,900
be sure not to stay
at the Hollywood Inn.

1074
00:40:13,600 --> 00:40:15,300
- Whoa,
she's having an episode.

1075
00:40:15,400 --> 00:40:16,333
- Geez, Moon, no.

1076
00:40:16,433 --> 00:40:19,467
- It's a huge
transistor radio.

1077
00:40:19,567 --> 00:40:21,333
- Send us up some ice.

1078
00:40:21,433 --> 00:40:23,100
- Send up some more
fruit soda.

1079
00:40:23,200 --> 00:40:24,100
And some chuckles.

1080
00:40:24,200 --> 00:40:27,133
- Huh? Yes, water.

1081
00:40:27,233 --> 00:40:29,700
Laugh juice.
Don't you know nothing?

1082
00:40:29,800 --> 00:40:31,067
Booze!
Yeah, lots of booze.

1083
00:40:31,167 --> 00:40:32,767
- Sid and Nancy.

1084
00:40:32,867 --> 00:40:34,233
- What do you mean?
Sure, we're old enough.

1085
00:40:34,333 --> 00:40:36,333
D'ya want to see
my driver's license?

1086
00:40:36,433 --> 00:40:40,467
Why, you--
Aghhh.

1087
00:40:40,567 --> 00:40:41,800
- What's up, man?

1088
00:40:41,900 --> 00:40:43,667
- Ah, that old dot
downstairs cut us off.

1089
00:40:43,767 --> 00:40:44,967
- Ahh, kids.

1090
00:40:45,067 --> 00:40:46,867
- Well, I know where we can
get all the lush we want, man.

1091
00:40:46,967 --> 00:40:47,867
- Where?

1092
00:40:47,967 --> 00:40:49,500
- It's about two hours'
drive from here.

1093
00:40:49,600 --> 00:40:50,667
- Oh, Hudson, Wisconsin?

1094
00:40:50,767 --> 00:40:52,800
- ...liquor store?
We can't stick him up.

1095
00:40:52,900 --> 00:40:54,133
His two weeks
ain't up yet.

1096
00:40:54,233 --> 00:40:55,833
[Laughing]

1097
00:40:55,933 --> 00:40:57,967
- [indistinct] man,
why don't you join the party?

1098
00:40:58,067 --> 00:40:58,967
What's the matter,
are you afraid

1099
00:40:59,067 --> 00:41:00,367
you might be
catching a cold, man?

1100
00:41:00,467 --> 00:41:02,300
- Maybe he just want to be
with that sweet little nothing

1101
00:41:02,400 --> 00:41:03,800
you've been
making eyes with, huh?

1102
00:41:03,900 --> 00:41:05,700
- Get off my back, Iris.
I'm thinkin'.

1103
00:41:05,800 --> 00:41:06,967
- Dreamin' is more like it.

1104
00:41:07,067 --> 00:41:08,867
You're dreaming how
you're gonna be a big fat star

1105
00:41:08,967 --> 00:41:10,733
and how well you and Helen
are gonna hit it off.

1106
00:41:10,833 --> 00:41:11,800
Isn't that it,
big shot, huh?

1107
00:41:11,900 --> 00:41:12,867
- Yeah, I'm big boned, okay?

1108
00:41:12,967 --> 00:41:13,867
- That's not right.

1109
00:41:13,967 --> 00:41:14,867
- Maybe you'd just
like to walk out on here

1110
00:41:14,967 --> 00:41:15,867
and you can forget
you ever knew us.

1111
00:41:15,967 --> 00:41:16,967
Isn't that it?

1112
00:41:18,533 --> 00:41:20,200
- I told you
to leave me alone.

1113
00:41:20,300 --> 00:41:22,433
- Next time, I'll punch you.
- Yeah, I got your message.

1114
00:41:23,700 --> 00:41:25,533
- I'm sorry.
I guess I just blew my stack.

1115
00:41:25,633 --> 00:41:26,967
[Knocking on door]

1116
00:41:27,067 --> 00:41:28,167
- I'll get it.

1117
00:41:28,267 --> 00:41:29,967
- The geeknik.

1118
00:41:30,067 --> 00:41:31,600
- Domino's.
- Yeah?

1119
00:41:31,700 --> 00:41:33,467
- I'm the hotel manager.
What's going on in here?

1120
00:41:33,567 --> 00:41:35,667
I've had complaints
from every room in the house.

1121
00:41:35,767 --> 00:41:37,533
- What's the matter, egghead?
Can't we have a little fun?

1122
00:41:37,633 --> 00:41:39,967
- Oh! Oh, my goodness,
what have you done to the room?

1123
00:41:40,067 --> 00:41:42,667
This is terrible.
Hey, you'll pay for this.

1124
00:41:42,767 --> 00:41:44,833
- My goodness,
you'll pay for this.

1125
00:41:44,933 --> 00:41:46,233
- Is that how I sound, really?

1126
00:41:46,333 --> 00:41:48,400
- You--
why, you young hoodlums.

1127
00:41:48,500 --> 00:41:49,433
I'll call the police.

1128
00:41:49,533 --> 00:41:51,200
- No magic pimpers
for you, young man.

1129
00:41:51,300 --> 00:41:53,867
- Say one word to anyone
and I'm gonna moon you.

1130
00:41:53,967 --> 00:41:55,967
- You're gonna what?
- Moon you!

1131
00:41:56,067 --> 00:41:57,600
- You know,
hang my butt out.

1132
00:41:57,700 --> 00:42:01,800
- You can rely on me.
I won't tell a soul.

1133
00:42:01,900 --> 00:42:04,533
But who's gonna pay
for the damage here?

1134
00:42:04,633 --> 00:42:05,533
- Just put it
on the bill, Mister.

1135
00:42:05,633 --> 00:42:06,833
I'll see it's taken care of.

1136
00:42:06,933 --> 00:42:08,067
- Thank you, sir.

1137
00:42:08,167 --> 00:42:11,000
- Now you get on out of here
before we change our mind.

1138
00:42:11,100 --> 00:42:13,867
- You can trust
in my discretion. I--

1139
00:42:13,967 --> 00:42:16,367
- Get!
- Sure.

1140
00:42:16,467 --> 00:42:18,767
- He's the shakiest
hotel manager in the west.

1141
00:42:18,867 --> 00:42:19,900
[Laughing]

1142
00:42:20,000 --> 00:42:21,667
- Boy, wasn't he scared?

1143
00:42:21,767 --> 00:42:24,367
Well, you can
trust my discretion.

1144
00:42:24,467 --> 00:42:25,500
- The next John Byner.

1145
00:42:25,600 --> 00:42:27,267
- ...calls the cops.
- He won't.

1146
00:42:27,367 --> 00:42:29,633
He's so chicken,
he could grow feathers.

1147
00:42:29,733 --> 00:42:31,933
[Laughing]

1148
00:42:32,033 --> 00:42:34,900
[♪♪♪]

1149
00:42:38,900 --> 00:42:42,433
[Singing]

1150
00:42:42,533 --> 00:42:44,433
- Oh, I'm so glad
Joel isn't here.

1151
00:42:44,533 --> 00:42:46,567
He'd just be ruining
everything right now.

1152
00:42:46,667 --> 00:42:49,000
Hey, are there any more
corn curls, Crow?

1153
00:42:49,100 --> 00:42:51,367
Crooooow?

1154
00:42:51,467 --> 00:42:53,133
- Crow T. Travis.

1155
00:42:53,233 --> 00:42:57,300
No, no.
Mrs. Tony T. Travis.

1156
00:42:57,400 --> 00:42:59,967
No?
No, too Italian.

1157
00:43:00,067 --> 00:43:03,633
Mr. and Mrs. Tony
and Crow Robot-Travis.

1158
00:43:03,733 --> 00:43:06,467
No, that's too long.

1159
00:43:06,567 --> 00:43:09,067
Wonder what Tony's
thinking about right now.

1160
00:43:09,167 --> 00:43:10,667
- Oh, I don't know.

1161
00:43:10,767 --> 00:43:12,767
He's probably
driving round real fast

1162
00:43:12,867 --> 00:43:14,867
in his super-cool car
and stuff like that.

1163
00:43:14,967 --> 00:43:16,100
Couldn't you just scream?

1164
00:43:16,200 --> 00:43:17,800
- Aghhhh!

1165
00:43:17,900 --> 00:43:20,733
- Oh, Tom,
you are so childish.

1166
00:43:20,833 --> 00:43:24,067
When you become a woman,
you'll understand these things.

1167
00:43:24,167 --> 00:43:27,000
The Tony I know
is a very serious man.

1168
00:43:27,100 --> 00:43:29,033
Compassionate
and thoughtful to a fault.

1169
00:43:29,133 --> 00:43:30,300
He goes to church
every Sunday.

1170
00:43:30,400 --> 00:43:31,500
- Wonder what denomination.

1171
00:43:31,600 --> 00:43:33,800
- Oh, please, Crow,
where d'you read that?

1172
00:43:33,900 --> 00:43:35,667
I just happen
to have the latest on Tony

1173
00:43:35,767 --> 00:43:38,967
in this month's "Tigerbot."
"Tony, fun-loving loner."

1174
00:43:39,067 --> 00:43:41,667
And it says, "Tony lives
with his parents in Burbank

1175
00:43:41,767 --> 00:43:43,433
"and loves to swap jokes
with Jay Osmond,

1176
00:43:43,533 --> 00:43:45,600
"the comedian
of the Osmond family.

1177
00:43:45,700 --> 00:43:47,933
"Sometimes you can find him
riding round the five acres

1178
00:43:48,033 --> 00:43:49,333
"behind his house
on his mini-bike

1179
00:43:49,433 --> 00:43:51,300
"or making funny faces
in the mirror

1180
00:43:51,400 --> 00:43:53,367
to crack himself up."
Ahh.

1181
00:43:53,467 --> 00:43:56,033
- I read in "Dynamite"
that he likes [indistinct].

1182
00:43:56,133 --> 00:43:57,933
- Oh, turn around, Gypsy.

1183
00:43:58,033 --> 00:44:00,500
Servo, you don't know
nothing about him.

1184
00:44:00,600 --> 00:44:03,500
Tony, and I know this
for a fact, girlfriend,

1185
00:44:03,600 --> 00:44:05,533
is producing
and starring and writing

1186
00:44:05,633 --> 00:44:06,667
and singing the theme song

1187
00:44:06,767 --> 00:44:08,100
for a movie about
his whole life story.

1188
00:44:08,200 --> 00:44:09,967
And on weekends, he's training
to be a Navy Seal.

1189
00:44:10,067 --> 00:44:11,133
- Oh, wow.

1190
00:44:11,233 --> 00:44:14,533
- Hey, so, guys, I got
all the rest of your stuff.

1191
00:44:14,633 --> 00:44:17,433
I think you're all settled in
for the evening now.

1192
00:44:17,533 --> 00:44:19,500
- Yes, Joel.

1193
00:44:19,600 --> 00:44:21,400
- You know what,
you guys are really into

1194
00:44:21,500 --> 00:44:24,167
this Tony Travis guy,
you know?

1195
00:44:24,267 --> 00:44:25,400
You know,
when I was your age,

1196
00:44:25,500 --> 00:44:28,033
that's when the teen idols
had faces, you know.

1197
00:44:28,133 --> 00:44:31,067
There was David Soul
and the Brady Girls

1198
00:44:31,167 --> 00:44:34,267
and Jeremy Gelbwaks
and Tony DeFranco

1199
00:44:34,367 --> 00:44:35,467
and the DeFranco Family.

1200
00:44:35,567 --> 00:44:36,900
Don't forget Donny Most.

1201
00:44:37,000 --> 00:44:38,667
- Spare us.

1202
00:44:38,767 --> 00:44:40,767
- You know, Tony Travis.

1203
00:44:40,867 --> 00:44:42,500
Now, wait a minute,
now that I think about it,

1204
00:44:42,600 --> 00:44:44,767
I think we went to
the same high school together.

1205
00:44:44,867 --> 00:44:45,767
- What?

1206
00:44:45,867 --> 00:44:47,467
- In fact, I think
I've got his number

1207
00:44:47,567 --> 00:44:48,733
right there on speed-dial.

1208
00:44:48,833 --> 00:44:51,133
It's marked "Tony T."
You should call him.

1209
00:44:51,233 --> 00:44:52,567
He's a real nice guy.
Go on, call him.

1210
00:44:52,667 --> 00:44:53,600
- No, no, no.

1211
00:44:53,700 --> 00:44:55,567
Oh, I can't do it,
I can't do it.

1212
00:44:55,667 --> 00:44:57,400
Hold it.
Should we?

1213
00:44:57,500 --> 00:44:58,800
- I'm gonna do it.
I'm gonna do it.

1214
00:44:58,900 --> 00:44:59,967
Tony T.

1215
00:45:00,067 --> 00:45:01,267
- I'm gonna die,
I'm gonna die.

1216
00:45:01,367 --> 00:45:03,167
I can't do this.
I need a shower.

1217
00:45:03,267 --> 00:45:05,267
Oh, oh, it's ringing,
it's ringing.

1218
00:45:05,367 --> 00:45:07,167
- Hello ?
- Oh, Tony.

1219
00:45:07,267 --> 00:45:10,333
- This is Tony Travis.
Sorry I'm not in right now.

1220
00:45:10,433 --> 00:45:13,833
I got called in to cover
for Roy over at the Taco Hell.

1221
00:45:13,933 --> 00:45:16,833
If everything goes right,
the sour cream gun don't jam,

1222
00:45:16,933 --> 00:45:18,700
should be home around 9.

1223
00:45:18,800 --> 00:45:20,367
If you'd like to leave
a message for me,

1224
00:45:20,467 --> 00:45:23,367
Gary, Rick,
Jeff, Rahoul,

1225
00:45:23,467 --> 00:45:26,367
Terry, Prairie Don
or any of the kids,

1226
00:45:26,467 --> 00:45:28,500
leave it
at the sound of the tone.

1227
00:45:28,600 --> 00:45:31,500
Or if you're a bill collector
or you're with the military--

1228
00:45:31,600 --> 00:45:32,733
[beeping]

1229
00:45:32,833 --> 00:45:33,800
- Oh, sad.

1230
00:45:33,900 --> 00:45:36,567
- No, can you believe it?

1231
00:45:36,667 --> 00:45:39,500
Oh, it is better
to have loved and lost

1232
00:45:39,600 --> 00:45:41,400
than never
to have loved at all.

1233
00:45:41,500 --> 00:45:42,467
